  "text": "**TASK_094: WebSearch Year Validation Implementation**\n\nAdded smart year detection to prevent Claude from searching for outdated years (e.g., \"TypeScript 2024\" when it's 2025).\n\n**Architecture Decisions:**\n- Extended existing pre-tool-validation hook rather than creating new hook (cleaner, single validation point)\n- WebSearch validation runs first, then file-based validations (logical separation of concerns)\n- Used regex patterns instead of LLM for performance (< 5ms vs potential 2-3s for SDK call)\n\n**Integration Points Identified:**\n1. Hook dispatcher (hook.ts:25) - Must route WebSearch to pre-tool-validation\n2. Hook function (pre-tool-validation.ts:269) - WebSearch-specific logic\n3. Settings.json - WebSearch PreToolUse matcher with 5s timeout\n4. Track.config.json - websearch_validation feature flag\n\n**Pattern Detection Strategy:**\n- 4 regex patterns cover common cases: end-year, start-year, latest/current, documentation\n- Separate isHistoricalSearch() for exemptions (comparisons, elections, temporal refs)\n- Returns suggested query in denial message for better UX\n\n**Files Modified (10 total):**\n- Core: pre-tool-validation.ts, hook.ts, types.ts\n- Config: settings.json, track.config.json, templates/track.config.json, init.ts\n- Tests: pre-tool-validation.test.ts (21 new tests)\n- Docs: README.md\n\n**Gotchas Discovered:**\n- Hook dispatcher easily forgotten - spent time debugging why hook wasn't running\n- Historical patterns need flexibility: \"2024 presidential campaign\" requires `\\w*\\s*` between year and keyword\n- Multiple integration points (dispatcher + settings) can cause silent failures\n\n**Code Review Outcome:**\n- Approved for production\n- All recommendations low-priority (future enhancements)\n- 95%+ test coverage estimated\n- No security or performance concerns",
